# Cross-zone source rewriting: a zone reaches into a LATER zone and edits its
# source text before it runs.
#
# `poke` pops three values -- zone index, character offset, character code --
# and rewrites that character in the target zone. Here zone 0 overwrites the
# `+` in zone 1 (at character offset 5 of its body) with a `*` (code 42).
#
# So zone 1 LOOKS like it computes 6 + 7 = 13... but actually prints 42.
{stack 1 5 42 poke}
{stack 6 7 + . }
